Ticket #4471 holds 412 reports about dates. It was merged as one issue, but it covers two
different bugs. Each got its own ticket.

## What was merged

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## What happened to each

| cause | what happens | outcome |
|---|---|---|
| parser | The shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants get a flipped month. | fixed: `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales` |
| hint | The booking-v3 form shows `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. People type month first, and the form reads it day first. | won't fix: booking-v3 form retired |

<Callout kind="warn">
The parser fix did not fix the hint bug. Closing #4471 as one issue would have hidden 33
reports behind a fix that never touched them.
</Callout>

## Notes

- Intake tags are a guess from the reporter's browser. In the parser group, 23 reports were
  tagged `hint`; in the hint group, 15 were tagged `parser`. Group by tenant and channel, not
  by intake tag.
- 5 parser reports read as a one-day move. The desk files them under `parser` by tenant and
  footnotes them.
- #4471 was merged by subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)).
  Matching subjects do not mean a matching cause.

